#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613134 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d9be18a-53c4-553d-8ef2-3b5c39d4d380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612653} {:answer/id #uuid "40df84b9-123d-54cc-ab20-d5c0b64fffbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612686} {:answer/id #uuid "bd9e2587-195f-5ed3-a248-e990e006ce81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612905} {:answer/id #uuid "ef7b50ee-8c8b-5001-b3e4-3fc0f3cf0cac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612989} {:answer/id #uuid "f4701e3f-859a-5abc-b934-2b616f605295" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613001}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612905} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b544fe5-a4d9-5998-bf81-77985c0ea42f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613053}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1ebd0d63-14bf-5fa5-b58f-5da92b5dc39e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97973" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A-4I)=0,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\text{nullity}(A-4I)=0$\n\nII. $A-4I$ is singular\n\nIII. $\\lambda =4$ is an eigenvalue of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{2} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=2=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $M$ has $2$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(M)+\\text{nullity}(M)=2.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. According to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(A-4I) & =2-\\text{rank}(A-4I) \\\\  & =2-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statements II is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A-4I)\\ne 0,$ we obtain that $A-4I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statement III is true. Notice that if $M=A-4I$ is singular, then $(A-4I)x=0$ has nonzero solutions which will be eigenvectors of $A.$ As a result, $\\lambda =4$ is an eigenvalue of $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33c55d74-ab99-5c5c-b558-e868a196633f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+4,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ x,\\, & x>1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612666} {:answer/id #uuid "35dc2b6d-d078-524e-bf54-b47ddd0dd5ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+4,\\, & x<2 \\\\ x,\\, & x>2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612669} {:answer/id #uuid "43753799-01f3-5daa-a412-c1c694610879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+4,\\, & x\\le 2 \\\\ x+1,\\, & x>2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612693} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0065f1-eba2-53ae-969f-5229db295741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4x,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ x+1,\\, & x>1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612804} {:answer/id #uuid "89bf0f2b-4c40-5a32-bb5f-590432d2bf40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The graph is not a function" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612832}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612666} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8d4aa2f-c2ed-59d0-95f0-ed9003e7e65a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "411b20bc-b7b4-5426-99f3-354ba829188a" :question/math-academy-id "q-6974" :question/problem "![](images/69/692b2beea671628e29269fd7ec481acafc17091b6c42afafc0c125cff32818d0.png)\n\nWhat is the definition of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We will graph each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,1],$ we have a line with a slope of $-1$ and $y$-intercept $4.$ So the graph is the line $y=-x+4$ that ends at $(1,3),$ including this point.\n\n- On the interval $(1,\\infty )$, we have a line with a slope of $1$ that passes through the point $(1,1).$ We can find the equation of this line using point-slope form:\n\n$$\ny-1=1(x-1)\\,⟹\\,y=x\n$$\n\nSo the graph is the line $y=x$ that starts at $(1,1),$ excluding this point.\n\nTherefore, the function is defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+4,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ x,\\, & x>1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "266d1298-b807-5d44-a7f4-f365fb5ad7d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/df/dfa8b6408bee2bdca1603f2071c5d52122083957c8d65ad9bfdbf61de7a6dd77.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612645} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf9dc89-38d9-5ebf-be0a-c6f32350ada8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e9/e9c0eb44b2e3bc20282042ec549ab7c6c9c558524b0503aaf5acbd71cb3ffc7e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612712} {:answer/id #uuid "b1985278-d43c-5d66-bd4f-9840c6fef78f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/40/406e0f0adb0a59eabae83f2e78f7db9b534c686b322ba633ffc41b712b213874.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612890} {:answer/id #uuid "d5dc09a7-0a09-58a3-b741-3f760315c943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fdb03315d54b7ba2a85a9260e1ba795d8f6ad06793a23ec580dcb737715cd05f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612944} {:answer/id #uuid "f0630e3e-6ca4-5cbc-ab3f-f316e4a1562e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/83/8378c30f9ea33f965a5d9415b8a2cc5b68d78a71943f9a97da4f67c2bb9ecf7b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612990}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612645} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc64ca2c-9158-5323-80f2-f548ea5f469e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4e3a84a5-3a49-5e84-8500-eff720b5fb31" :question/math-academy-id "q-46791" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\,,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ -1\\,,\\, & x>1\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following is the graph of $y=f(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "We will graph each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,1],$ we have $f(x)=2,$ so the graph is a horizontal line that ends at $(1,2),$ including this point.\n\n- On the interval $(1,\\infty )$, we have $f(x)=-1,$ so the graph is a horizontal line that begins at $(1,-1),$ excluding this point.\n\nTherefore, the graph of the given function is as follows:\n\n![](images/df/dfa8b6408bee2bdca1603f2071c5d52122083957c8d65ad9bfdbf61de7a6dd77.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e2ab068-3c30-5221-9c68-9dd40942b569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f$ and $h$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612626} {:answer/id #uuid "64426e60-1879-5d38-8898-b89154d98f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$h$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612759} {:answer/id #uuid "9e7bd7bc-892f-5b55-9372-1286ec0e9d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$g$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612859} {:answer/id #uuid "bf1e58a0-d439-59cc-8f9e-ba539d4f05cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f,$ $g,$ and $h$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612906} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb1e499-c441-55d1-836a-8d7e85eed9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613020}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612626} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bf8df05-0e7f-51cc-8068-e3691b4e8795" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "721af26d-c8a1-5cd7-a08a-18d41b317c1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-110864" :question/problem "Let $D=[0,1]\\times [0,2].$ Which of the following functions are valid joint probability density functions?\n\nI. $$\n\\displaystyle f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2-xy}{3},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nII. $$\n\\displaystyle g(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-y}{4},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIII. $$\n\\displaystyle h(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1\n$$\n\nLet's check the above conditions for each of the given functions.\n\n- The function $f$ is a valid probability density function. Indeed, we have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$  and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2-xy}{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2-xy}{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{4x-{x}^{2}y}{6}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{4-y}{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[4y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $g$ is *not* a valid probability density function because it does not satisfy the first condition. For example,\n\n$$\ng(1,2)=\\frac{1-2}{4}=-\\frac{1}{4}≱0\\,\\times\n$$\n\n- The function $h$ is a valid probability density function. Indeed, we have $h(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$  and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}h(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}h(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{x}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{y}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$f$ and $h$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613202 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fbf60cd-78c9-5731-a8ef-1e03331e953a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0c/0c67f5eb270cf274a144d1ceb2dba835746dded1cd671c7f3f9b10583c9e860c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612657} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc68304-3c41-57f9-9d12-1fe3c74e5f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/46/467e330d6851443618bfad78582e3b9086b32b2a33d082779ddee9a902076d29.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612801} {:answer/id #uuid "83b94dac-e42c-5094-8531-d5660567490d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b5/b5f9401d386fe30ad342820d712138607bffa94529663b3f5160573548c7eefd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612816} {:answer/id #uuid "bca6f2c5-4ca6-57dc-a544-f139bc5fc6df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3f/3f62687f8eedfb27934221612d154c59e3c5321c495e428086dc48ae53958b0b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612904} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6d5ce0-8180-55cc-b0f2-6e291f66375d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/97/9747b0337f36a0aaea267c71c6c25ca7dd5341983035e0d0ebbb1d3e16d4f931.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612957}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612904} :answer-field/id #uuid "89575e3a-fd68-532f-9f6a-e3337ebf360b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d499a293-3ad3-5177-9700-3f04240373d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-46792" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\,,\\, & x<-1 \\\\ -1\\,,\\, & -1\\le x<1 \\\\ 2\\,,\\, & x\\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following is the graph of $y=f(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "We will graph each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,-1),$ we have $f(x)=2,$ so the graph is a horizontal line that ends at $(-1,2),$ excluding this point.\n\n- On the interval $[-1,1),$ we have $f(x)=-1,$ so the graph is a horizontal line that begins at $(-1,-1),$ including this point, and ends at $(1,-1),$ excluding this point.\n\n- On the interval $[1,\\infty ),$ we have $f(x)=2,$ so the graph is a horizontal line that begins at $(1,2),$ including this point.\n\nTherefore, the graph of the given function is as follows:\n\n![](images/3f/3f62687f8eedfb27934221612d154c59e3c5321c495e428086dc48ae53958b0b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613203 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ab0c308-8721-5697-af3f-f5c8cfb71b4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1\\,,\\, & x<2 \\\\ -1\\,,\\, & x\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612706} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad4a45c-dc97-5561-a289-2c88748c273a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1\\,,\\, & x\\le 2 \\\\ -1\\,,\\, & x>2.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612708} {:answer/id #uuid "91ece1cb-88a5-5905-875f-7002b002e0b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\,,\\, & x\\le 0 \\\\ -2\\,,\\, & x>0.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612845} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a977c7-5812-51df-84d1-f1054880eddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\,,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ -2\\,,\\, & x>1.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612915} {:answer/id #uuid "f3320494-2120-5d15-ad1e-2c38fd11f25d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\,,\\, & x<1 \\\\ -2\\,,\\, & x>1.\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186612999}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186612915} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0bf2648-2b22-5b57-a6ba-11eea164ef4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d5eb57be-dfbd-536c-b378-d7b234bb6108" :question/math-academy-id "q-46884" :question/problem "![](images/50/50080eb76ea9afaf62f137968fc2383420bed9ab34311d381cae9b712d9e3194.png)\n\nWhat's the definition of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above, given that $f(x)$ is defined for $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )?$" :question/worked-solution "We will determine each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,1],$ we have $f(x)=2.$ Notice that the point $x=1$ is included.\n\n- On the interval $(1,\\infty )$, we have $f(x)=-2.$ Notice that the point $x=1$ is excluded.\n\nHence the definition of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\,,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ -2\\,,\\, & x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613736 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07b03764-a089-5a4d-a66a-31329f7d792c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1557" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613308} {:answer/id #uuid "17694358-54ab-5a63-adf5-7ca72ab3e375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1589" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613326} {:answer/id #uuid "4f75cb7a-3697-55b8-b0dd-e83121f6bad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1313" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613402} {:answer/id #uuid "c91978bf-50fc-534b-935b-c4b2abb01ab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1697" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613571} {:answer/id #uuid "dc904223-b70e-5699-87a9-ffbcd902046c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1403" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613590}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613590} :answer-field/id #uuid "de4c79b5-5159-5f1e-98e9-debc73c7710c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "04158aea-4871-56e3-8054-9fc9c287146a" :question/math-academy-id "q-96423" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{1}{9}\\right),$ calculate $P(10\\le X<15).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}\\left(\\frac{1}{9}\\right).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{-x/9}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(10\\le X<15)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(10\\le X<15) & ={\\int }_{10}^{15}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{10}^{15}\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{-x/9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/9}{|}_{10}^{15} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-5/3}+{e}^{-10/9} \\\\  & ≈0.1403\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613751 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a19f5fa-0de4-516b-8cfc-400d9302ffbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613311} {:answer/id #uuid "334594f5-5ece-54de-8bfb-d5563cc94dd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613363} {:answer/id #uuid "6a68b1af-7c3d-53dc-9bf8-d1e185969e41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613444} {:answer/id #uuid "92fa6039-dda6-56ed-8bc8-b563232760f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613491} {:answer/id #uuid "f2de921b-947c-55f8-82fc-8f85f235372a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613614}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613614} :answer-field/id #uuid "653dc8eb-dc79-5139-9725-108d7e68173a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "34d42fc7-8828-5a45-9815-dbd48a905e3c" :question/math-academy-id "q-143577" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}), & -1\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expected value of $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The marginal density function for $Y$ when $-1\\le y\\le 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=-1}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}[\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {1}^{3}+1\\cdot {y}^{2}-(-\\frac{1}{3}-{y}^{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}(\\frac{2}{3}+2{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{4}, & -1\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $Y$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}y\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{4})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(\\frac{y}{4}+\\frac{3{y}^{3}}{4})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{3{y}^{4}}{16}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{3}{16})-(\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{3}{16}) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613800 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50e899c2-5160-5ea5-815e-556d32ee7f2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613405} {:answer/id #uuid "5ed0085d-fb0b-58da-9d21-9156693da86c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613421} {:answer/id #uuid "73334a67-5ecf-5954-9fda-bd7dab220535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613453} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e9097f-f1cc-5a04-8215-56fdb120e4d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613542} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b864a9-6dbc-5552-9dbb-0305f8e8094a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613565}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613542} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb6758ca-e43b-5fda-8655-92a5f89de056" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613723}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cbdf796d-50c0-5849-8726-3912e57b8aa4" :question/math-academy-id "q-143578" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}, & x\\ge 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expected value of $X.$" :question/worked-solution "The marginal density function for $X$ for $x\\ge 1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{6{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}}{[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}{[{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}({1}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the  expected value of $X$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }x\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\lim_{b\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{b}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\lim_{b\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{1}^{b} \\\\  & =2\\lim_{b\\to \\infty }(1-\\frac{1}{b}) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613802 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14b5b705-d3dd-5c04-856d-0d79cad656b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613321} {:answer/id #uuid "3912e235-410d-5acc-80ad-ab38393b639b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2281" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613371} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbfc1c5-853b-53ff-b3da-fd6f60fd3eeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2371" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613506} {:answer/id #uuid "acb0c673-aae0-5ae5-9f17-3c34248ec0e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2333" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613526} {:answer/id #uuid "c25cf1cc-a39d-5475-9a2b-7d5c8510bea4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2231" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613561}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613561} :answer-field/id #uuid "d688208d-6573-531b-bba5-e2ec8c9b7dde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d6c1611d-d019-58e6-b404-0000cc88bbef" :question/math-academy-id "q-132186" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(1.5),$ calculate $P(X\\ge 1).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(1.5).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1.5{e}^{-1.5x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X\\ge 1)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 1) & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }1.5{e}^{-1.5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1.5x}{|}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-1.5} \\\\  & ≈0.2231\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186614589 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e512c56-e236-5d6a-91aa-a023e899499f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}(x-8)(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613917} {:answer/id #uuid "2339a515-3aad-5299-bf43-74ca2603b800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}(x-8)(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613964} {:answer/id #uuid "38dbd142-86c5-5bb5-8f41-5cd2cdaecfd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}(x-4)(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614010} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc86bcf-9c70-5843-8530-9358fdc9b718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9(x-8)(x-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614077} {:answer/id #uuid "9dadfaa5-7001-5220-97d7-ac5202b30a3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}(x-4)(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614212}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613917} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e8048f-ade3-56c0-ba20-8eb72c827560" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "70b715c1-5950-56ba-a3d5-3b39dfaf8df1" :question/math-academy-id "q-126153" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{9}(5-x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<2 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $2\\le x\\le 5,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ {\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{x}\\frac{2}{9}(5-t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={(\\frac{10}{9}t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{9})|}_{2}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{10x}{9}-\\frac{16}{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}({x}^{2}-10x+16) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}(x-8)(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{9}(x-8)(x-2), & 2\\le x\\le 5 \\\\ 1, & x>5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186614624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ac0f5b8-f15a-5613-93a8-66720c136903" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.314" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613984} {:answer/id #uuid "7c236059-6b63-59f9-a83f-f09fa2f4b64d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.217" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614129} {:answer/id #uuid "942300de-23f8-5bd9-b73a-a7accb74ba7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.196" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614196} {:answer/id #uuid "9e273ba9-afe8-50a9-94da-8a81d0bece4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.551" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614214} {:answer/id #uuid "ac10ab50-b42a-5b20-8b30-8ebda33afd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.054" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614244}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186614196} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a54e5e4-2593-5da2-83e2-0ecda10d87ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614461}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c0646aa3-5fbe-58eb-868d-e19bf4c41735" :question/math-academy-id "q-131257" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈1.0265,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & 1\\le x<2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{1}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =1.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & ≈1.25-(1.0265)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.196.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186615380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75e30e16-40f6-5476-a98b-57a19c157d94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614943} {:answer/id #uuid "8a516247-3827-5aea-9d55-efe7a74fa192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614986} {:answer/id #uuid "b85d5366-cbc6-5f0c-a391-c3e8269ab5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615074} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f81533-0f8f-5035-be7e-a977791fe2bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615102} {:answer/id #uuid "f8aa242e-6e75-5914-bb84-7c321d9e7075" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615186}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186615186} :answer-field/id #uuid "fefcfc19-0bd6-5c0b-86c8-d42a0a2e2ba1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615351}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2167bad9-800b-5e62-ab30-44c746dfa55b" :question/math-academy-id "q-143824" :question/problem "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}, & x=0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}, & x=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{4}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{4}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each cubed value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{4}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}+{1}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}+{2}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =0\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}+1\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}+16\\cdot \\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{16}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616956 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11608109-63f4-5381-863e-6e92792cc660" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616410} {:answer/id #uuid "70ead1a7-c4f0-5c8f-b43c-6dc1d4b49e9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616574} {:answer/id #uuid "8d64e571-5d10-561a-ab42-498565eee28f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616623} {:answer/id #uuid "c9871779-87ac-5527-9f77-c162b9fc5de2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616740} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcdff5c-fc94-5c25-ad88-bd265bf3a798" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616768}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616410} :answer-field/id #uuid "a65d4c6c-16b6-5e9e-beb1-c18412078827" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2dc2fed3-d655-5205-951d-af8d7bb52e4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-142473" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and  $det(A)=0?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col)}(A)=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null)}(A)=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. A matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=0,$ our matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $A$ is *not* invertible, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible,  it must be $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ffa830c-d80c-50f1-a9d5-fe1ebcd7331a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616472} {:answer/id #uuid "74e42cb9-e4af-5881-b608-c6f11cb10b48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616580} {:answer/id #uuid "a7630b66-b242-57a5-9ee0-cb303aa7fd5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616679} {:answer/id #uuid "b0012022-5d79-54b1-9714-0e41233affc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}^{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616695} {:answer/id #uuid "ffae7155-96c2-535c-bde8-3a20e9b83925" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616821}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616695} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a148ab1-c122-59b6-a4a9-dfb8bdba9c0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9c53dbaf-3ce4-5d86-a287-de9fed2a2135" :question/math-academy-id "q-141193" :question/problem "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)=\\bbox[3pt,white,border:2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is ${R}^{n}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04c50643-01aa-57fa-8703-551f411bcef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616382} {:answer/id #uuid "341e787a-6216-56d1-addd-83742093725f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616459} {:answer/id #uuid "bc33d81e-9442-5b3d-9e29-5ebf4f6366a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616713} {:answer/id #uuid "d5396c66-36ca-5609-9c8e-2f99af1e2e6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616758} {:answer/id #uuid "e3317a2c-6551-5c55-9f93-e3277b68058b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616775}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616775} :answer-field/id #uuid "48d03ec9-bb33-5a1b-9a2d-866361f6881e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a20e0f6e-9a4b-59f0-b28f-3a10b5209120" :question/math-academy-id "q-141205" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. All columns of $A$ are pivot columns\n\nIII. $Ax=0$ has no non-trivial solution" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nSince $det(A)\\ne 0,$ the matrix $A$ must be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n,$ which means that all columns of $A$ are pivot columns.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then $Ax=0$ has no non-trivial solution.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\},$ which means that $Ax=0$ has no non-trivial solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617034 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02717221-4f50-5e06-99ab-b59d6c370818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616376} {:answer/id #uuid "4362c2da-1b14-5a05-82ec-cd9d02715c27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616481} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e5b857-ddf6-57fa-9bba-e751dd4041cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616681} {:answer/id #uuid "c3aeddf3-6a3f-5940-a84a-a0d812268bed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616728} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ca4f0f-0cea-584c-9154-5654b6b76388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616781}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616681} :answer-field/id #uuid "2903c293-1eda-5011-b735-91c9fbb84274" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f35a0916-c2f9-5592-8918-2772549e2c23" :question/math-academy-id "q-141197" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=6$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ is invertible because $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since,\n\n$$\n\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{dim(Col}(A))=5.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is invertible,  it must be $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617780 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "092ca6d8-81bf-5c26-9cf7-8a0c9bd00db4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617261} {:answer/id #uuid "0ab38e3c-3dab-5e4a-baef-22455182b4aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617265} {:answer/id #uuid "1a7525d0-f772-54b5-aa6c-0148776aaea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617293} {:answer/id #uuid "3f709820-3513-52a4-a948-2ac1bfea560e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617371} {:answer/id #uuid "73de121c-460e-5c93-9b8c-c7defddf2dbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617439}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617439} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a7cda4b-7199-5307-8542-f1f1d7f89182" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617670}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1225e989-4806-5aac-9651-4963cdc92720" :question/math-academy-id "q-90645" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-5,1],$ compute $P(-3<Y<0).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $Y$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le y\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-5,1],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6},\\, & -5\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-3<Y<0) & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}\\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{0-(-3)}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05205eee-681d-5372-abdb-27cd25c2790c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617250} {:answer/id #uuid "67359505-d2f5-5099-a050-9d5f0338e832" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617424} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed64918-017f-5939-bee9-cbc0de3907c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617486} {:answer/id #uuid "d77fb7d0-b6a4-5b51-9168-b5477e127c47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617605} {:answer/id #uuid "ea4bd99c-e394-5aae-b196-562495f4cd0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617638}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617250} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ec89339-8a37-511c-9b4a-1c07649b3446" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1b9005f5-505d-5f29-9792-9b464932d844" :question/math-academy-id "q-130537" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,0],$ compute $P(X\\le -1).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,0],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3},\\, & -3\\le x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le -1) & =P(-3\\le X\\le -1) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-(-3)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617795 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "760de2c7-eb3e-5ae9-9b41-a62a595afb31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617441} {:answer/id #uuid "981d2c25-4478-590c-b6d9-d88014351d37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617497} {:answer/id #uuid "9df1cb8a-80bc-5bed-81b8-ae8e90d5c809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617506} {:answer/id #uuid "adab90c5-f9f6-5ff4-9a39-cede2c282479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617533} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7c17fc-038c-56db-ad31-fdecb047e227" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617556}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617506} :answer-field/id #uuid "27ee8578-df69-590f-8cdc-14ade2064bb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3a7fe469-3903-50db-8722-b3f6155142b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-96338" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,-5],$ compute $P(-9<X\\le -6).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,-5],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5},\\, & -10\\le x\\le -5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-9<X\\le -6) & ={\\int }_{-9}^{-6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-9}^{-6}\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{-6-(-9)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617802 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dbbdc3f-5d4e-5db7-aa2d-a4b04bfe0506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617433} {:answer/id #uuid "99bc81bd-ce95-5820-a272-c45037be3aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617499} {:answer/id #uuid "a86d0e75-2c30-59cf-be6c-f49cb1e3d738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617521} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8a6968-cdf7-5078-a425-4e4c904fbddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617586} {:answer/id #uuid "eee2e290-8326-5d0e-8ff7-66ac4a8859ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617642}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617499} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f89fb87-5f0e-552a-b3b3-b99ff5535836" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "43000328-4a22-57f5-bdf3-0abcdf581fbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-96289" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-5,10],$ compute $P(Y\\ge 0).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $Y$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le y\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-5,10],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{15},\\, & -5\\le y\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\ge 0) & =P(0\\le Y\\le 10) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{10}f(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{10}\\frac{1}{15}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{10-0}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617807 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122e7d18-1853-5ba7-b4dd-17b7b9358740" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617282} {:answer/id #uuid "376a5df7-18e7-51d7-a0bf-13e85fd1871f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617357} {:answer/id #uuid "4df301ba-f7a2-5b0d-9e25-7ab56dcb2a5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617393} {:answer/id #uuid "7c26fea1-e915-55f5-b642-fa4c42947932" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617453} {:answer/id #uuid "bba50734-158f-57eb-a6c3-544b70e0c627" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617557}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617453} :answer-field/id #uuid "85832e8d-6935-5f35-9993-0aca10224a15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4be83071-6e78-5b94-ae1e-aabad0413f90" :question/math-academy-id "q-90635" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-2,5],$ compute $P(X>1).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-2,5],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7},\\, & -2\\le x\\le 5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1) & =P(1<X<5) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5-1}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cd7a270-c923-5321-b03b-91294b0c851a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617272} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2196f4-2899-53d8-a8c5-175355f1d4f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617397} {:answer/id #uuid "cb313136-3435-5806-b49d-55f8141168bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617585} {:answer/id #uuid "df2afb8b-bb2b-52a1-b1e1-bb6cc551c3d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617616} {:answer/id #uuid "e76756f2-09eb-5fb9-aa44-234c28ffe9ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617635}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617272} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd3dbd79-ba23-5ce5-97db-ee10adf20d8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8abf9b68-45ee-59ee-bf5c-359348bee405" :question/math-academy-id "q-130549" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-6,-2],$ compute $P(-5\\le X<-3).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-6,-2],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & -6\\le x\\le -2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-5\\le X<-3) & ={\\int }_{-5}^{-3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-5}^{-3}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-(-5)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df4d76b-d9eb-5cf6-b303-ec66233f4322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617278} {:answer/id #uuid "21ca45d2-7791-5884-9b4f-8056a9efa6ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617311} {:answer/id #uuid "43ad0f4f-c5ff-5fcb-980a-c8209d1a6fee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617375} {:answer/id #uuid "b2a31807-dc04-5507-b026-744aedff0c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617540} {:answer/id #uuid "fe288a64-79ba-513a-9f04-9f55a393d4c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617664}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617278} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c86b770-099e-5dc6-bd38-a0e45a33cc06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617706}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b1d5ffaa-6323-5539-b03d-e56382198099" :question/math-academy-id "q-96285" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ compute $P(W\\le 1).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{3}{2}],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{3}{2}\\le w\\le \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\le 1) & =P(-\\frac{3}{2}\\le W\\le 1) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3/2}^{1}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617847 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0848772f-2f70-5071-aef3-c835c16edef5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617259} {:answer/id #uuid "162a5331-790c-5228-a756-f241465a9779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617285} {:answer/id #uuid "8430abe4-d622-5115-99d8-52093e6a978a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617468} {:answer/id #uuid "87802c7a-c6bf-5df2-bb6d-3cf46a62bb21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617471} {:answer/id #uuid "f5177445-1e10-5e83-bb45-122e7230d709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617650}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617259} :answer-field/id #uuid "882c95cb-0302-5bef-a28c-48371d8f7a7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b87148c7-0deb-51d1-a0cd-bc86a5be535f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96283" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[1,2],$ compute $P(Y\\le \\sqrt{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $Y$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le y\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[1,2],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le \\sqrt{3}) & =P(1\\le Y\\le \\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}f(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618729 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19d88783-092f-50f2-a548-a2aae6f77037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618246} {:answer/id #uuid "3f04f55d-63d7-51cb-9426-0ce8b82a86cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618303} {:answer/id #uuid "7661a999-43cd-5664-83fb-3c75db378d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{69}{133}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618376} {:answer/id #uuid "79b77f02-6ff4-5f79-afef-59711fa8c1d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{191}{399}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618383} {:answer/id #uuid "d49d0dcf-eb9d-522d-a521-384932bf795d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{133}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618524}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618376} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac3c3e6d-c759-511c-9361-ab7212b30272" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618664}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "25a65043-d221-5005-946b-5de5010791ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-146382" :question/problem "A high school has $400$ students enrolled. Of this student population, $48\\%$ use the school bus. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the population uses the school bus} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $i=1,…,400.$ Find $P({X}_{2}=0|{X}_{1}=0).$" :question/worked-solution "We have a population of size $N=400,$ and $p=0.48$ represents the proportion of the population that uses the school bus.\n\nTherefore,\n\n- the number of students who use the school bus equals\n\n$$\nNp=400(0.48)=192,\n$$\n\n- the number of students who do not use the school bus equals\n\n$$\nN(1-p)=400(1-0.48)=208.\n$$\n\nWe select two students at random. We need to find $P({X}_{2}=0|{X}_{1}=0),$ the probability that the second student does not use the school bus given that the first student does not use the school bus.\n\nIf the first student does not use the school bus, we have\n\n$\\,$ $N-1=400-1=399$ students remaining, and\n\n$\\,$ $N(1-p)-1=207$ students remaining who do not use the school bus.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP({X}_{2}=0|{X}_{1}=0)=\\frac{N(1-p)-1}{N-1}=\\frac{207}{399}=\\frac{69}{133}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618765 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "176d570f-7314-54ff-a3f4-1d25a05a5d93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{159}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618241} {:answer/id #uuid "1aefb8b5-2219-5ce6-8a77-ab85160149c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{53}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618250} {:answer/id #uuid "4fd258b2-21a8-5c01-9a62-f96b3eaa2797" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618326} {:answer/id #uuid "80f34643-1d62-506a-b19d-c99f48507019" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{159}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618395} {:answer/id #uuid "a637c7d9-72df-59d3-873d-d4b3a5c01a23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618453}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618241} :answer-field/id #uuid "aba11c03-5d04-5be2-8a79-600209cb0b33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "735101d7-417c-5654-90c3-00d2eafdbcaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-146375" :question/problem "A language school has $160$ students enrolled. Of this student population, $15\\%$ are bilingual. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the population is bilingual} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $i=1,…,160.$ Find $P({X}_{2}=1|{X}_{1}=1).$" :question/worked-solution "We have a population of size $N=160,$ and $p=0.15$ represents the proportion of the population who are bilingual.\n\nTherefore,\n\n- the number of population members that are bilingual equals\n\n$$\nNp=160(0.15)=24,\n$$\n\n- the number of population members that are not bilingual equals\n\n$$\nN(1-p)=160(1-0.15)=136.\n$$\n\nWe select two members of the population at random. We need to find $P({X}_{2}=1|{X}_{1}=1),$ the probability that the second member is bilingual given that the first member is also bilingual.\n\nIf the first member is bilingual, we have\n\n$\\,$ $N-1=160-1=159$ members remaining, and\n\n$\\,$ $Np-1=23$ members remaining who are bilingual.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP({X}_{2}=1|{X}_{1}=1)=\\frac{Np-1}{N-1}=\\frac{23}{159}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622783 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37979d26-53d8-5296-9f32-d90a23c5682a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622404} {:answer/id #uuid "aa125ea2-b3f8-56f3-98af-ffe69580bb85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622558} {:answer/id #uuid "b855949f-83e3-524b-b182-322e49afafa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622572} {:answer/id #uuid "bb5fffa4-2e2d-5ea7-baa8-d5144df0719a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622578} {:answer/id #uuid "c90570f9-701e-5471-93fd-c0ddf315c480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622593}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622404} :answer-field/id #uuid "027afff5-46c9-57d1-a11e-fd920d125d36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4eee1aa8-16ff-553d-83f1-a811ba095524" :question/math-academy-id "q-159305" :question/problem "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0\\,\\text{or}\\,y<1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}(y-1)}{y}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 1 \\\\ {F}_{Y}(y), & x>1,\\,y\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the joint PDF $f(x,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the partial derivatives of $F(x,y)$ are defined, the joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂x∂y}F(x,y).\n$$\n\nFor $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $y\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\frac{{∂}^{2}}{∂x∂y}F(x,y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}(y-1)}{y}\\right)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(1-\\frac{1}{y})) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOtherwise, $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,y\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622811 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2138ab3d-e180-5050-b430-2ac769b26cda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{1-x}}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622376} {:answer/id #uuid "52a9a2f5-feb4-576d-940d-08f9ba289613" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}-{e}^{1-x}+\\frac{{e}^{1-x}}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622435} {:answer/id #uuid "9badb244-9a6e-5338-b092-3a0d2ef2d324" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}+\\frac{{e}^{1-x}}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622536} {:answer/id #uuid "a4733a34-81aa-50d9-b1fd-004f1e7a8691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{{e}^{1-x}}{{y}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622549} {:answer/id #uuid "cec22405-503a-5840-bfc8-ec390a4cdbaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}-{e}^{1-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622599}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622435} :answer-field/id #uuid "49da5325-2128-58a0-920f-928be9342ee8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "996c08b9-0c9d-50b6-8d3d-4ba4a7be0327" :question/math-academy-id "q-159317" :question/problem "The marginal CDFs of two continuous independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{1-x}, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}, & y\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the joint CDF when $x\\ge 1$ and $y\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are independent continuous random variables with marginal CDFs ${F}_{X}(x)$ and ${F}_{Y}(y),$ respectively, then the corresponding joint CDF of $F(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)={F}_{X}(x)\\cdot {F}_{Y}(y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $x\\ge 1$ and $y\\ge 1,$ the joint CDF for our random variables is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x,y) & ={F}_{X}(x)\\cdot {F}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =(1-{e}^{1-x})(1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}-{e}^{1-x}+\\frac{{e}^{1-x}}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the joint CDF is\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}-{e}^{1-x}+\\frac{{e}^{1-x}}{{y}^{3}}, & x\\ge 1,\\,y\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186625561 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f7f8479-5350-5313-8b2e-9c517e2873e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625053} {:answer/id #uuid "7a396e4d-b7e4-5133-a086-dc50e972fbb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625096} {:answer/id #uuid "9845855a-bfef-54a3-8406-9c6b66538b28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625147} {:answer/id #uuid "a87b9014-d2b2-5d92-9c5a-427eabbb8806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625176} {:answer/id #uuid "c62f1bc4-0d82-5af0-b00e-6c5da3bf3a43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625238}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186625096} :answer-field/id #uuid "29daf4fc-e24e-5065-92f4-f3e5525c95d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "963787a0-af1d-590d-a99b-bb7022b3057b" :question/math-academy-id "q-87233" :question/problem "Compute $P(X\\ge 8)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 8) & =P(8\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{8}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}]}_{8}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186625569 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55134816-77f3-5101-82d2-eb76d70dbdb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625036} {:answer/id #uuid "67f1da11-8f0d-5955-bc8d-02231d399544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625067} {:answer/id #uuid "87e4ad28-5e06-5710-966e-1bf8042ac1c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625123} {:answer/id #uuid "95dcdba2-bbbb-54f6-85e4-08d7046505f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625139} {:answer/id #uuid "ccbc81cc-0a6a-533a-af29-5646af6b4b30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625253}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186625139} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd64f7c4-a1ad-5dfc-8858-e400dc900d3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625484}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a398441f-b3fc-5349-9fd8-52ae9a922241" :question/math-academy-id "q-160468" :question/problem "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{x+1},\\, & x\\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ defined on a set $S$ to be a valid probability density function, it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\n$$\n\nIn our case, for the function $f(x)=k{e}^{x+1}$ on the interval $x\\le 1,$ the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}k{e}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{1}k{e}^{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x &=k{e}^{x+1}\\,{|}_{-\\infty }^{1}=k{e}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this result back into the first equation and solving for $k,$ we get\n\n$$\nk{e}^{2}=1\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186625585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d119e01-9f41-5db1-b328-cc80d83fe116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625017} {:answer/id #uuid "62078149-64f7-5037-85c3-eef9a84bf60e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625058} {:answer/id #uuid "a726da00-0364-5998-824a-5efa3f1d04e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625170} {:answer/id #uuid "bda169b6-7124-5af5-8f8b-4222223e87cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625221} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d7b03c-13ea-54cd-add6-ea802da2a17d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625332}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186625332} :answer-field/id #uuid "0818581a-2e92-50b3-a75b-774a611fb6ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186625364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c5248bd6-3abb-5040-8044-89eb68f5d62f" :question/math-academy-id "q-87224" :question/problem "Compute $P(X\\ge 6)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}},\\, & x\\ge 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 6) & =P(6\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{6}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}]}_{6}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "217d00e3-6085-5217-9e0f-bc0ed267a659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627152} {:answer/id #uuid "4d216911-9fdd-5d94-9372-99c99ec03e85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627226} {:answer/id #uuid "c69e47ba-4ae4-5ccc-94e3-da31c8bee3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627431} {:answer/id #uuid "cb083657-c6c3-5e24-8fd7-4d2f8e37c426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627440} {:answer/id #uuid "d61c0f82-de33-5eb0-80d0-e768ca91585e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627460}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627440} :answer-field/id #uuid "5be541ef-8f3c-5ccd-a814-640b71ca741c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "48e66ecf-d81b-50c1-a8a1-a9e2ad76a682" :question/math-academy-id "q-141217" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$\n\nIII. $det(A)=0$" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{nullity}(A)=0.$* $\\,\\times$\n\nBy the invertible matrix theorem, if  $\\text{Col}(A)$ is not ${R}^{n}$ then  $A$ is not an invertible matrix and  so we must have $\\text{nullity}(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, if  $\\text{Col}(A)$ is not ${R}^{n}$ then  $A$ is not an invertible matrix and  so we must have $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then  $det(A)=0.$* $\\,✓$  \n\nSince $\\text{Col}(A)⊂{R}^{n},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ is not invertible, which means $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e0fc9f-7385-5c7b-ae3b-103b9330e3c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627091} {:answer/id #uuid "1c378646-9302-5a64-9728-c1b51529df79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627145} {:answer/id #uuid "708def97-75ed-58ef-a2bf-6861c83ab912" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627282} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8fd432-6f8f-51c7-bfbb-559a7ea21b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627354} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c36613-e9d3-5ba7-91ca-a44714c54624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627371}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627091} :answer-field/id #uuid "48b9389d-612d-5d40-ba4a-42e4e4c73b9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "624ebabe-0dfa-5173-b265-5c678170209c" :question/math-academy-id "q-142478" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n\nIII. $Ax=0$ has only the trivial solution" :question/worked-solution "If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{3} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then  $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$* $\\,\\times$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=3=\\text{rank}(A).$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ invertible matrix,  then $Ax=0$ has only the trivial solution.* $\\,✓$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\},$ which means that $Ax=0$ has only the trivial solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627711 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b67416e0-aaf4-5cd6-ad03-e199f73af9eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{468}{3125}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627390}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627390} :answer-field/id #uuid "15d82638-6d44-54da-9f1d-d22206a0efa3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627552}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8c423a5c-7505-5f32-8017-eb441412608b" :question/math-academy-id "q-334514" :question/problem "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.6),$ compute the **exact** value of $P(2<X\\le 5).$\n\n$P(2<X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.6),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(0.4)^{x-1}(0.6), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 5) & =P(X\\in \\{3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=3)+P(X=4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =f(3)+f(4)+f(5) \\\\  & =(0.4)^{2}(0.6)+(0.4)^{3}(0.6)+(0.4)^{4}(0.6) \\\\  & =0.14976.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627712 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f3616d-847e-5517-a188-3bcfbeff8d44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5348" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627216}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627216} :answer-field/id #uuid "8227a0ac-9a1e-584d-9ec6-dcee9ff0f23b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9d9c5439-ddcf-55a1-834c-99b4bc6d083c" :question/math-academy-id "q-335459" :question/problem "Given that $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.34),$ compute $P(1<X<6)$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.\n\n$P(1<X<6)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.34),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(0.66)^{x-1}(0.34), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<6) & =P(X\\in \\{2,3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=2)+P(X=3)+P(X=4)+P(X=5) \\\\  & =f(2)+f(3)+f(4)+f(5) \\\\  & =(0.66)^{1}(0.34)+(0.66)^{2}(0.34)+(0.66)^{3}(0.34)+(0.66)^{4}(0.34) \\\\  & ≈0.5348.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627715 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2db7a114-79ca-5bba-8124-a7181493b13b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{rank}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627175} {:answer/id #uuid "3d068235-7187-58b5-8e9a-5227645c538c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Col}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627198} {:answer/id #uuid "5962a640-dcc7-5027-bb07-b17fe801639b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{dim(Col}(A))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627245} {:answer/id #uuid "988e139f-a77f-5b44-b4d1-f1beefdeed76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{Null}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627350} {:answer/id #uuid "a129ec1b-a9f3-52d1-9974-a86f524b2b4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{nullity}(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627363}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627363} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d11f370-8031-53e9-948e-0abb973068db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a697d815-4993-501b-8fbd-3b051df82a6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-141195" :question/problem "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\bbox[3pt,white,border:2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\text{nullity}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627728 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029e31b7-ff5b-561b-aa12-1b5e6a2a8a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9963" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627095} {:answer/id #uuid "5e059f51-34c3-573b-9ba6-8ad892ce88b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9630" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627255} {:answer/id #uuid "609eec15-ffb1-5c97-afc5-c3fe7c1faca2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.9031" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627258} {:answer/id #uuid "8937e429-2ee0-5d72-a3b0-869138e45ea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8529" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627328} {:answer/id #uuid "9d5560e1-ab32-50c4-aced-d95a6a067b5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7828" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627356}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627255} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b9673f3-5781-5a1e-9911-480a1cedda7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c23f992c-a4e0-564f-8888-ec13b671c121" :question/math-academy-id "q-97137" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right),$ compute $P(X\\le 3).$  Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{x-1}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & ={\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{0}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)+{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{1}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)+{\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)}^{2}\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) \\\\  & ≈0.9630.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627730 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b2ef5d6-4e27-5b2f-803d-6a89b80fd4e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.147" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627221}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186627221} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd57ab95-6415-5782-81cf-94e18ffe9fbd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186627646}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ca540711-a61f-5010-8af2-d0821eec16a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-331520" :question/problem "Given $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.3),$ compute $P(X=3).$\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle P(X=3)=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.3),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}(0.7)^{x-1}(0.3), & x=1,2,3,… \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & =(0.7)^{2}(0.3) \\\\  & =0.147.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186628493 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20cef65e-896d-51d2-bf70-a3d36f560f67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628041} {:answer/id #uuid "59ea468d-1248-5736-9514-88204cd5fa0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628115} {:answer/id #uuid "73af6ff6-7339-5494-9b14-4724ebc1e103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628144} {:answer/id #uuid "78696590-18a2-55d3-bf49-c58513a6ed0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628148} {:answer/id #uuid "adc1821a-5b17-5501-a7e1-04812a563de6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628231}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186628115} :answer-field/id #uuid "c129a918-c961-50ec-9d7d-aa112246fa8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c083c22d-506a-5bd7-88e8-ae0eb0acb960" :question/math-academy-id "q-152910" :question/problem "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}, & x\\le 0 \\\\ {x}^{2}, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $f(x)?$\n\nI. $f(x)$ is defined at $x=0$\n\nII. $\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)$\n\nIII. $\\lim_{x\\to 0}f(x)=f(0)$\n\nIV. $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "To test for continuity of $f(x)$ at a point $x=c$, we need to check three conditions:\n\n1\\. Does $f(c)$ exist?\n\n2\\. Does $\\lim_{x\\to c}f(x)$ exist?\n\n3\\. Does $\\lim_{x\\to c}f(x)=f(c)?$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Using the expression for the first branch of the function, we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(0)=-(0)^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=0.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is true. By calculating the one-sided limits, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & =\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{-}}(-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-(0)^{2} \\\\  & =0 \\\\ \\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & =\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =(0)^{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=0$ exists:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 0}f(x)=0\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we have that $\\lim_{x\\to 0}f(x)=0=f(0).$  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since all statements I-III are true, according to the continuity test, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"All the statements are true.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186635493 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10d86352-fe0f-585e-82d8-21e03bb43ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634859} {:answer/id #uuid "689a2d63-a4e4-533d-a926-20cb1b5a8ea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635033} {:answer/id #uuid "9a4ef3d5-ee76-5c23-a44a-8a6feef6c831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635145} {:answer/id #uuid "a677b2b2-5288-583a-ad88-3a7fef8adca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{10}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635166} {:answer/id #uuid "d82aab7d-70e6-5997-b4d8-c96d9a1072af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635258}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186635145} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ffa8b30-2c5b-5c54-b14d-0df3abc07b24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4e379040-f6ed-56bd-95b5-1c098fef9fe8" :question/math-academy-id "q-142910" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-(x+y)}, & x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(-1\\le X<10).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) &={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\\,{f}_{Y}(y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $X$ for $x\\ge 0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(x) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-(x+y)}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-(x+y)}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\infty } \\\\  & =0+{e}^{-(x+0)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for ${f}_{X}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1\\le X<10) & ={\\int }_{-1}^{10}{f}_{X}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{10}{e}^{-x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-x}]}_{0}^{10} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-10}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186635497 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ffd6481-248d-527d-8664-ccf57198c0c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2325" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186634994} {:answer/id #uuid "83479c19-62b5-547b-ae49-f501d5274008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2152" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635094} {:answer/id #uuid "92a8a9b5-d228-5180-acf3-7a7620ba622a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2285" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635129} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b5434d-dff1-5d8a-85ff-41cbecdd2784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2035" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635155} {:answer/id #uuid "ef88052f-5b66-50d7-8e19-6ac27bf4cc13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2226" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635307}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186634994} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f54527c-b99d-577c-9de4-6407cda9b78d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "591965f1-c329-5af7-bae1-27542c4e3d2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-132197" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $W∼\\text{Exp}(0.5),$ calculate $P(2\\le W\\le 4).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $W$ with rate $\\lambda$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda w}, & w\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nW∼\\text{Exp}(0.5).\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.5{e}^{-0.5w}, & w\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(2\\le W\\le 4)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le W\\le 4) & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}0.5{e}^{-0.5w}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =-{e}^{-0.5w}{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{-1} \\\\  & ≈0.2325\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636450 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aae8e56e-b620-565e-8e1b-dea16c081961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636080}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636080} :answer-field/id #uuid "4070e2f0-7227-50dc-9a65-ec2161067e86" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22c11e36-344f-5d90-aafe-2f3a2c4a03dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635830}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186635830} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1897272-e294-5268-a0e3-469cfd190698" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636372} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca8e58fa-e6b9-5aca-a07f-f91a7539e2fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636148}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636148} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1520759-ff14-5d38-964c-6dd3fb4f3379" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636394}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3ed231f7-1b89-5fd7-abb2-02b96f820104" :question/math-academy-id "q-220265" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}16+3x>31 \\\\ 2-3x\\ge -16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\le$\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $x$ that satisfy both $16+3x>31$ and $2-3x\\ge -16$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $16+3x>31\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16+3x & >31 \\\\ 16+3x-16 & >31-16 \\\\ 3x & >15 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & >\\frac{15}{3} \\\\ x & >5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/cd/cd42f4b10d78e5426affc38098dd95748ba1442294181f6637f2755c093ad0af.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $2-3x\\ge -16\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-3x & \\ge -16 \\\\ 2-3x-2 & \\ge -16-2 \\\\ -3x & \\ge 18 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-3x) & \\le (-1)\\cdot (-18) \\\\ 3x & \\le 18 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & \\le \\frac{18}{3} \\\\ x & \\le 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/20/205d97f5ac2f372e95bccc50af875dcc818b4c3f057d43b136ae0eb253e64a58.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/be/be869912c57a1002771b078718c2086730fd0867f29e23a68934b2e128862df0.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $5<x\\le 6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636456 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "129ef573-c987-5452-a89f-dfd43bc443cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635794} {:answer/id #uuid "1fbb4194-1218-54be-bd19-e71697da2e8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635826} {:answer/id #uuid "672d83ff-c90f-56d9-a167-b36cc77ffab9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$y<-2$ or $y\\ge 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635968} {:answer/id #uuid "cefc1902-3b36-5b2b-a9ad-1610a2436474" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636158} {:answer/id #uuid "f4dd6ced-8e67-55eb-b77c-d5592496441c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All real numbers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636248}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186635794} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea6586f2-96bd-56f7-b1fe-a3dc5e42f476" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "461355df-ddac-5bf6-9494-89a7687a4dba" :question/math-academy-id "q-156120" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3y+2\\ge 8 \\\\ 4y-1>-9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $y$ that satisfy both $3y+2\\ge 8$ and $4y-1>-9$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $3y+2\\ge 8\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y+2 & \\ge 8 \\\\ 3y+2-2 & \\ge 8-2 \\\\ 3y & \\ge 6 \\\\ \\frac{3y}{3} & \\ge \\frac{6}{3} \\\\ y & \\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/73/73bd7382587a92294b22b26cd0838a817ecab8c125ccae9babe01ac39195b561.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $4y-1>-9\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-1 & >-9 \\\\ 4y-1+1 & >-9+1 \\\\ 4y & >-8 \\\\ \\frac{4y}{4} & >\\frac{-8}{4} \\\\ y & >-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/f0/f0dba5cf289573a50499d4013cbe42449b3054bf78b513839fb2875e1feb3f20.png)\n\nTo find the values of $y$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/99/99e2870523abca60bea27ce1e90c27385cd2c86ec6918d1db6d0e018a39621f9.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $y\\ge 2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636457 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "632e9f05-2dbb-5c00-828e-2d8ecda59d4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e2/e2351e9c6265dda8f7965385c11c1dead47b6ecc4e2fa3fbfb9478b1531e4b80.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635958} {:answer/id #uuid "80058acc-9a71-56e9-849f-bbd4664698bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9c/9c53865226dce7874be62fa41ca0b4803150376d750c6a730212b1773283ee27.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636011} {:answer/id #uuid "ba480bef-2abf-58f8-abc8-41eb7f092e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636106} {:answer/id #uuid "cc5ef05b-4ffe-522b-9a16-b5f4b3994d90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/90/901981ec764aa655cc3fcc5be2f5769daa1eae9f53dbe624543bfea1c40d3cec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636154} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ddaa42-365a-58a5-869e-6ca73fd988ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ce/cea4298beb20e551dc294512c5c31bb723501e153317f06a9f78e24a782d8d39.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636219}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636106} :answer-field/id #uuid "0993fb68-8904-5dac-be7d-c4fb3186a590" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "46b9e7c9-accf-544f-901c-1d4419b679bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-156150" :question/problem "Which number line shows the solution of the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}t-1<-3 \\\\ 7t+6\\ge 20\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $t$ that satisfy both $t-1<-3$ and $7t+6\\ge 20$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $t-1<-3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t-1 & <-3 \\\\ t-1+1 & <-3+1 \\\\ t & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/40/40af0183e4619cb1c638b956ed37abc987508db0582254dfb79a179e6656b5cc.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $7t+6\\ge 20:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7t+6 & \\ge 20 \\\\ 7t+6-6 & \\ge 20-6 \\\\ 7t & \\ge 14 \\\\ \\frac{7t}{7} & \\ge \\frac{14}{7} \\\\ t & \\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ae/ae24cb18655db0d4d3a8b6a7c5033ffdbc1b7bc6ad8a6d339e9c14c5faa57688.png)\n\nTo find the values of $t$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap: \n\n![](images/b5/b549a9ec68930c51878b22842e576f3f2edcf1290f73bc571e721b759a7a696a.png)\n\n   \n\nIt turns out that the solutions do not overlap at all. Therefore, there are no values of $t$ that satisfy both inequalities simultaneously. So, there is no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636488 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "987e9d61-a518-5b61-b141-029cf3239dcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636053}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636053} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfe98b15-625b-5f29-a8e1-64dfddcc430a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "411a03c2-daf1-5645-8f3f-2e9d52d88890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635889}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186635889} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0618fc5-25ec-5117-98ab-7201e73cd2ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8e759e25-031b-5302-b0b8-f76d4a70c525" :question/math-academy-id "q-218747" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+17>53 \\\\ 9x-8\\ge 37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $x$ that satisfy both $6x+17>53$ and $9x-8\\ge 37$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $6x+17>53\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+17 & >53 \\\\ 6x+17-17 & >53-17 \\\\ 6x & >36 \\\\ \\frac{6x}{6} & >\\frac{36}{6} \\\\ x & >6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/05/05974b618a70f290c3d31620f8356ef8b3b1f07a91875eb330deb7f766a9703a.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $9x-8\\ge 37\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-8 & \\ge 37 \\\\ 9x-8+8 & \\ge 37+8 \\\\ 9x & \\ge 45 \\\\ \\frac{9x}{9} & \\ge \\frac{45}{9} \\\\ x & \\ge 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/d2/d220bf5c2225964e06a63b7242093a4589fa10793c1fd9f0e880acb023aa36ee.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/58/58ea0840e901f55c653cba24bcac12caaf490ad2615200af92bcadfa44f5f83c.png)\n\n \n\nThus, the final solution is $x>6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636491 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6adcc707-dbee-5a09-8031-67b29c50d82a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635977}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186635977} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eed335f-113a-5adf-bad2-4c9bff54c7c0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636307} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b01519fd-4115-5a94-a039-3344a7e10e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636083}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636083} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0978602-e328-55fa-b070-41a92d97abf3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51e87984-d723-5685-8d5f-3a55e33aab0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635921}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186635921} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea626f83-7463-5559-9f11-26b69788d1fd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "94c02e7f-8a0a-5248-8c16-140d78b5a296" :question/math-academy-id "q-220263" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}20z-34>26 \\\\ 19-2z>-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$z<$\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $z$ that satisfy both $20z-34>26$ and $19-2z>-3$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $20z-34>26\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20z-34 & >26 \\\\ 20z-34+34 & >26+34 \\\\ 20z & >60 \\\\ \\frac{20z}{20} & >\\frac{60}{20} \\\\ z & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/87/87ffa3967e575b95b1e5b78d2ce71888fe28f817039469546659c432ce92abe7.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $19-2z>-3\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}19-2z & >-3 \\\\ 19-2z-19 & >-3-19 \\\\ -2z & >-22 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-2z) & <(-1)\\cdot (-22) \\\\ 2z & <22 \\\\ \\frac{2z}{2} & <\\frac{22}{2} \\\\ z & <11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/8f/8f9aeb83f08164584c9425be871722f9b8622a44d57575a4224de44185fb0185.png)\n\nTo find the values of $z$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/8b/8b7a52e58eb73a5158148d2b6bde4394c290af01ab20540d10bd1c7d83f1ca97.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $3<z<11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636492 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f77c34b7-924c-5cce-914a-9625c71598f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "<" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636260}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636260} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ba766a3-7268-5722-b0d4-04e828077546" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636290} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e16a8a5-b76b-57f1-b823-c8f6bfa0c00d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635983}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186635983} :answer-field/id #uuid "74ff81a9-653d-5df9-a08a-1cd1ce16c8c9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b340563-8043-5c4b-9fa1-623a5a5ff6b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635811}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186635811} :answer-field/id #uuid "e21313f3-bfbe-5b99-9738-9f59f0bc5625" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "95cdc902-ee39-5f50-928f-92f405d3459a" :question/math-academy-id "q-218702" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}14x-6<8 \\\\ 6x+5\\ge -13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $x$ that satisfy both $14x-6<8$ and $6x+5\\ge -13$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $14x-6<8\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14x-6 & <8 \\\\ 14x-6+6 & <8+6 \\\\ 14x & <14 \\\\ \\frac{14x}{14} & <\\frac{14}{14} \\\\ x & <1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/20/20f1a72c65c584f04291df953b5d7a39c78283e923560283c02a9a07ab7ef083.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $6x+5\\ge -13\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+5 & \\ge -13 \\\\ 6x+5-5 & \\ge -13-5 \\\\ 6x & \\ge -18 \\\\ \\frac{6x}{6} & \\ge \\frac{-18}{6} \\\\ x & \\ge -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/b1/b1f1baf7621290e93ec7a22101ebbd089c3765766d24648d9f565d0d80999b7f.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/47/47039330f87aaaf6763a02f72cdea49bbb3e9e3989ea02cbe5a40258b1c35dd5.png)\n\n \n\nThus, the final solution is $-3\\le x<1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636511 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20c79210-9a2c-5647-b164-c7daec6c0a8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635828} {:answer/id #uuid "404eb17f-05d8-5df1-8103-75cd8112897e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p\\in [-3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635886} {:answer/id #uuid "528d05f2-290f-58e2-baa4-78ce4a200ec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p\\in [-3,-1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635924} {:answer/id #uuid "633f3099-3548-5b47-a17a-a21aa31758ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p\\in (-3,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635959} {:answer/id #uuid "d356493c-3aef-5d6c-b848-5c5725314804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p\\in [1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636170}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186635959} :answer-field/id #uuid "0aa21e84-0980-531a-99e6-38cc9d73607e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cd620146-d7c3-5e8f-8f0a-f0f089c81645" :question/math-academy-id "q-156071" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}p+5>2 \\\\ 4-2p\\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $p$ that satisfy both $p+5>2$ and $4-2p\\ge 2$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $p+5>2\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p+5 & >2 \\\\ p+5-5 & >2-5 \\\\ p & >-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/b5/b5e98b482f45c224c0e634866a4a5e5ae4011fd3d7d34a4ee4d68741e0a2dbde.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $4-2p\\ge 2\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-2p & \\ge 2 \\\\ 4-2p-4 & \\ge 2-4 \\\\ -2p & \\ge -2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-2p) & \\le (-1)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 2p & \\le 2 \\\\ \\frac{2p}{2} & \\le \\frac{2}{2} \\\\ p & \\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/56/562e666633ff53a2eb1a450740e6cd13182ee74ee9d930b3d008e9c0b943b3b8.png)\n\nTo find the values of $p$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/f3/f36f7475ec5f310295684246be455881a4d693e745a621ceb4413dd9f3b6ba12.png)\n\n \n\nThus, the final solution is $p\\in (-3,1].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636535 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ac78ed8-0059-51ff-bce0-141f574fa42e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m\\in (-4,-2]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186635976} {:answer/id #uuid "7a112f65-11c3-58cc-a884-c5094fdaa212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m\\in (-4,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636005} {:answer/id #uuid "8bdd0c69-463f-53bd-b0a9-bafc550f2523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m\\in (-2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636034} {:answer/id #uuid "d617f2a8-05f5-54ff-a8b0-919a3b1da53b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There is no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636176} {:answer/id #uuid "f395b39d-43e3-50c1-9848-b9ecc80729bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m\\in (-4,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636244}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186636034} :answer-field/id #uuid "27e188f6-ea48-5a3a-9de9-c87284920d72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186636302}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fb1d51a3-f351-5c78-b2ef-3f9d4e574ba3" :question/math-academy-id "q-156117" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}m+3<7 \\\\ 2-3m<8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $m$ that satisfy both $m+3<7$ and $2-3m<8$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $m+3<7\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m+3 & <7 \\\\ m+3-3 & <7-3 \\\\ m & <4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/62/628ef6f170fa8029151a50c60b20075f267981f779383264e7f3d5d50ad4f5c5.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $2-3m<8\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-3m & <8 \\\\ 2-3m-2 & <8-2 \\\\ -3m & <6 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-3m) & >(-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\ 3m & >-6 \\\\ \\frac{3m}{3} & >\\frac{-6}{3} \\\\ m & >-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/fc/fca54780fcdfcfead46b629d41b0bf1607db5ef34256d2225777e8d50c7c87e3.png)\n\nTo find the values of $m$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/b3/b3abcd21a153010151989379f30b091bb9068a542a34d1cbd103ef66be9129b5.png)\n\n \n\nThus, the final solution is $m\\in (-2,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639256 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06fcd619-8b14-57e1-93e9-787c0407681b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638638} {:answer/id #uuid "24653554-6ad7-5735-b6ee-6d0b173453e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638695} {:answer/id #uuid "828bbb08-2b85-5a7c-8cc8-4a802d2ce02a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638853} {:answer/id #uuid "b400eccf-d163-50c8-af18-1ee088d84763" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638946} {:answer/id #uuid "ce52120b-1e45-5820-aedb-61df3a11ab89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638993}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186638853} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4ba750b-4dfe-54a9-88bb-ffdbb22fb964" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e5389cec-a648-50b1-b04e-06a01b9f0c7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-67898" :question/problem "Find $\\lim_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}-2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡(x+1)\\, & \\text{ for }\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To compute $\\lim_{x\\to \\,(1/2)}f(x),$ we must compute the left and right-sided limits separately.\n\nHowever, the left-sided limit $\\lim_{x\\to \\,(1/2)^{-}}f(x)$ does not exist since $f(x)$ is not defined on the interval $x\\in (-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}).$ \n\nConsequently, the overall limit does not exist either:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (1/2)}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639267 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c485f09-a154-5c3b-9072-5ff2524fcb5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{x\\to 0}f(x)=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638678} {:answer/id #uuid "25374503-2624-5f88-9b23-dd66c353770d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{x\\to 0}f(x)=\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638697} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd966a1-7bf9-5605-bdc7-7e0e787628c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{x\\to 0}f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638763} {:answer/id #uuid "7501d3ae-6d1c-5ee9-9b19-63c97c64c613" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{x\\to 0}f(x)=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638829} {:answer/id #uuid "c4767ede-816a-5a16-bbc3-c94da1bf5cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lim_{x\\to 0}f(x)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186638976}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186638697} :answer-field/id #uuid "036887cd-f8cf-5ce6-b154-383b53276d9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ff29de00-f9ee-5524-adfb-762bca88101b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36708" :question/problem "Find the limit at $x=0$ for the function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<0 \\\\ 2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x=0 \\\\ 3\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Approaching from the left, we have $x<0,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{-}}x=0\\,.\n$$\n\nApproaching from the right, we have $x>0,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=3.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)=\\lim_{x\\to {0}^{+}}3=3\\,.\n$$\n\nSince the two limits are different, we can conclude that \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to 0}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642290 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f1ca290-7691-5a59-b4a9-0ed704dfff8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641906} {:answer/id #uuid "56c6b5ca-9d6c-5db7-b06e-2828055e72b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641962} {:answer/id #uuid "5e946f31-88ae-5fcb-8b00-0ad96c140580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641977} {:answer/id #uuid "66d965d2-3809-5c55-9b96-2854197e46a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641987} {:answer/id #uuid "e36e7c6b-1cda-584c-94cd-111be574d0e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642160}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642160} :answer-field/id #uuid "4053447b-7ead-5696-b940-bb0d92cf2247" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "024f763e-73c5-5093-a984-85656a0fb11d" :question/math-academy-id "q-125771" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the probability density function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{-4x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le m) & ={\\int }_{0}^{m}4{e}^{-4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-4x}{|}_{0}^{m} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-4m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-4m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {e}^{-4m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -4m & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\ -4m & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ m & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642296 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7482e6c4-f76f-5b46-ae70-a0d17bb593c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.179" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642005} {:answer/id #uuid "9418a158-49a1-5bfe-a20e-b1e74e2fcffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.630" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642058} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ab70fe-f840-578a-8e04-4893acda98f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.279" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642081} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c31a70-0e0a-551f-a7da-8935e6e272fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.239" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642149} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a4e283-3f87-5740-9b62-fe16405e02b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.909" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642158}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642081} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca6b31fe-6c68-5239-827b-835c9af25951" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642274}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1573f6d2-e6b3-5110-b9d1-e35d2c482d87" :question/math-academy-id "q-125710" :question/problem "Find, to three decimal places, the interquartile range of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0, \\\\ {x}^{3},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 1,\\, & x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the interquartile range, we first need to find the lower quartile and the upper quartile.\n\nThe lower quartile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${q}_{1}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{1})=\\frac{1}{4},\n$$\n\nand the upper quartile is the number ${q}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {q}_{3})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the lower quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{1}) & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {q}_{1}^{3} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {q}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the upper quartile:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ F({q}_{3}) & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {q}_{3}^{3} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ {q}_{3} & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{3}{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the interquartile range is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}IQR & ={q}_{3}-{q}_{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{3}{4}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{4}} \\\\  & ≈0.908\\,560-0.629\\,961 \\\\  & ≈0.279\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4761115a-653a-5f0c-826c-ce005081317a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641945} {:answer/id #uuid "7dea5dca-8a88-5b82-b218-c3fab1c50d5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642022} {:answer/id #uuid "8e44cb0d-0d8d-59d6-bc9d-432c2be0e227" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642050} {:answer/id #uuid "c3725af8-6b21-56e5-b3af-72bef455da04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642111} {:answer/id #uuid "d3c73064-776d-5d71-b997-47ff970d63b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{2.5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642141}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642022} :answer-field/id #uuid "e08f9eb3-7268-52bd-b3dc-82f960b974de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7081d182-b8d8-55ec-b299-e610f160df11" :question/math-academy-id "q-94580" :question/problem "Find the $12.5$th percentile of the random variable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${x}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {x}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $12.5$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.125.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {x}_{0.125}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{{x}_{0.125}}\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{27}|}_{0}^{{x}_{0.125}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{0.125}^{3}}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $12.5$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}_{0.125}^{3}}{27} & =0.125 \\\\ {x}_{0.125}^{3} & =(0.125)(27) \\\\ {x}_{0.125} & =\\sqrt[3]{(0.125)(27)} \\\\ {x}_{0.125} & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642342 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e3be216-12a2-589e-94de-de419d8bcc4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641843} {:answer/id #uuid "0fc11e7d-bc98-5369-bfb8-6cd6a265ba07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641846} {:answer/id #uuid "36aa94ae-6c25-540e-9be0-df6b5c0a4a1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641919} {:answer/id #uuid "5b8febe6-442c-5a09-a6c4-2429d55dfbb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641974} {:answer/id #uuid "77ec063e-3401-5930-bfd2-a0278115a8ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642012}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186641974} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b485620-4675-5393-986c-2c3267a2b268" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8e093d1b-62df-5413-8e2c-75bf77f8c95f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94703" :question/problem "Find the $80$th percentile of the random variable $Y$ if the probability distribution function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}},\\, & y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $Y$ is the number ${y}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le {y}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $80$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.8.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le {y}_{0.8}) & ={\\int }_{1}^{{y}_{0.8}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={-\\frac{1}{y}|}_{1}^{{y}_{0.8}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{y}_{0.8}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $80$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{1}{{y}_{0.8}} & =0.8 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}_{0.8}} & =0.2 \\\\ {y}_{0.8} & =\\frac{1}{0.2} \\\\ {y}_{0.8} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642358 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d282a98-16a5-5263-abac-7a369fcd2549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641904} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd773c7-61d7-5d7a-8fa2-947a23f3a74a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641907} {:answer/id #uuid "3c26f182-11b1-5090-b53a-93b6aa2a80a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641932} {:answer/id #uuid "65a93096-0909-52bd-ae3c-f95d2626bb66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641984} {:answer/id #uuid "c103b06f-5891-58a0-8aaa-534c2b75af34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642108}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186641907} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c4aa0d7-4f63-5480-8032-496b37d48a18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b38e8e22-1127-597c-af47-702704300221" :question/math-academy-id "q-94634" :question/problem "Find the median of the random variable $Y$ if the probability density function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{1-y},\\, & y\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The median of a random variable $Y$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(Y\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le m) & ={\\int }_{1}^{m}{e}^{1-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-{e}^{1-y}{|}_{1}^{m} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{1-m}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{1-m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {e}^{1-m} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1-m & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\\\ 1-m & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ m & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644074 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "358c69b3-ddb5-5632-b4ea-93f4a71dfb8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643610} {:answer/id #uuid "3791aebc-39f7-5ba1-b955-9972b52e5a82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643614} {:answer/id #uuid "49b38dca-b6fc-57e1-ad10-06517374334a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643640} {:answer/id #uuid "701dd6ec-3daf-58cc-9501-3af69d76ad91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643719} {:answer/id #uuid "ed5efbf3-e548-5e8b-8e3e-68682f3ac70a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643942}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643614} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e4df0e3-695a-57e2-8bc4-8a0831a5e650" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "186f1cf8-7438-580a-834c-470ece90c857" :question/math-academy-id "q-147841" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y\\sqrt{x}}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The joint support of $X$ and $Y$ is given by the rectangle \n\n$$\nS=[0,1]\\times [0,3].\n$$\n\nMoreover, we can write \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=g(x)\\cdot h(y),\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{3}$ and $h(y)=y.$ \n\nTherefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent, and consequently $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37bb92c3-318e-5d23-9331-74186e4eef57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643616} {:answer/id #uuid "66f6f6cd-666d-5d57-ae56-049f4bb6bd78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643696} {:answer/id #uuid "7c7be86a-1d5c-570a-a2c9-4994237d4de8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643737} {:answer/id #uuid "d416bc29-37f3-55df-8596-59477312807c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643894} {:answer/id #uuid "f2287b2c-6a71-5cbd-b61f-98cfe948b9e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643950}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643737} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ddd7e38-6074-579e-b026-e802378be85f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2cacc419-42ec-5cb5-af14-357c84e44a7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-147842" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4y}{(x+1)^{2}}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The joint support of $X$ and $Y$ is given by the rectangle \n\n$$\nS=[0,1]\\times [0,1].\n$$\n\nMoreover, we can write \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=g(x)\\cdot h(y),\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}$ and $h(y)=4y.$ \n\nTherefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent, and consequently $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644092 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "157bb6bd-eb34-5755-ab9c-f02551155554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643549} {:answer/id #uuid "1f6720a8-a654-5f84-9ca6-40fffcd4e237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643571} {:answer/id #uuid "26277bbc-6c69-541b-b9d0-c3e64fd2094b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643584} {:answer/id #uuid "2a299248-d2e1-5d38-a7f4-3da1d7e19428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}xy" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643591} {:answer/id #uuid "577ec71f-9f4b-5a54-861e-8114b46976ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643667}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643549} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f5180bf-98e6-5761-b477-86adf1b8dbf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4638055e-14fd-5846-abac-04d24e583b2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-143661" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x>1,\\,y<0.$" :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables with the joint probability density function $f(x,y),$ then the corresponding joint CDF is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(X\\le x,Y\\le y)={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v.\n$$\n\nLet's draw the region $D$ in the $uv$-plane where the function $f(u,v)$ is nonzero. Let's also consider a point $(x,y)$ where $x>1,\\,y<0,$ and a region $Δ$ that lies below and to the left of this point.\n\n![](images/4e/4eb1ddc9c6e47da6cfc8de92184208c4b433ea622d7241fda5c5fca2acee566a.png)\n\nFor the purposes of computation, we're only interested in the region inside $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. This is given by\n\n$$\nD\\cap Δ=∅.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo there is nowhere in our region $Δ$ where $f(x,y)$ is nonzero. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{y}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v & ={∬}_{Δ}f(u,v)\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dc5559a-cea3-597d-8b2b-d304f278af35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643599} {:answer/id #uuid "42e35278-47ce-5fa4-bb15-4a75311cd1e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643628} {:answer/id #uuid "44f2dfe9-17b2-5448-be81-986d12dec13c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643633} {:answer/id #uuid "d22a7241-6e13-534e-a5df-ae3704720d8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643891} {:answer/id #uuid "e19b99d2-f07d-5a18-bbdb-7401c5f74518" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643920}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643599} :answer-field/id #uuid "eae47f43-493d-5b4c-a997-90e4e70e06d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6c677c0e-b320-572a-874f-19f411142323" :question/math-academy-id "q-147845" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{5}{8}$ and $\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{5}{8},$ calculate the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The covariance of $X$ and $Y$ can be calculated using the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nTo find $\\text{E}[XY],$ we use the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xyf(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}y{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}+x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}y{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}y[\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{3}{8}y+\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{2}+\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the covariance formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}-\\left(\\frac{5}{8}\\right)\\left(\\frac{5}{8}\\right) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644149 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16cdb97f-c925-516c-9e23-fffb5aed3d76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643551} {:answer/id #uuid "4f750833-c57b-5fbe-8164-f229b97e0cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643652} {:answer/id #uuid "7b303090-1875-535f-b8e3-be023efb4f2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643735} {:answer/id #uuid "ca05f123-fd69-5271-8224-6cc3fad8aee0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643876} {:answer/id #uuid "cbc3e851-2e5f-5600-971b-e77b6b5a615b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643878}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643735} :answer-field/id #uuid "b26941a6-4389-5a09-b64c-8bfc871e8650" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d597cf7a-d27a-5d2c-b4de-9bdb7767a3e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-147843" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{64}{9\\,{x}^{3}{y}^{3}}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "The joint support of $X$ and $Y$ is given by the rectangle \n\n$$\nS=[1,2]\\times [1,2].\n$$\n\nMoreover, we can write \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=g(x)\\cdot h(y),\n$$\n\nwhere $g(x)=\\frac{64}{{x}^{3}}$ and $h(y)=\\frac{1}{9\\,{y}^{3}}.$ \n\nTherefore, $X$ and $Y$ are independent, and consequently $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186644163 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14cf4fbb-c58a-59ea-9a55-2089554db319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643547}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643547} :answer-field/id #uuid "625548d5-f75f-564a-857a-0721fa3d7f83" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cc8c1b2-56af-59e2-ae81-d65402f33ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186643708}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186643708} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ab4bed1-1856-52c1-9a7f-c00e67627773" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186644030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f30b451d-2977-5471-a648-9e6a3210577b" :question/math-academy-id "q-218750" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4z+1>-3 \\\\ 9z+13\\ge 76\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is\n$z$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $z$ that satisfy both $4z+1>-3$ and $9z+13\\ge 76$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $4z+1>-3\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4z+1 & >-3 \\\\ 4z+1-1 & >-3-1 \\\\ 4z & >-4 \\\\ \\frac{4z}{4} & >\\frac{-4}{4} \\\\ z & >-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/f2/f28d14912f9c153fcabb15643cbe2a116ab2174a1897d58644872f884179a28e.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $9z+13\\ge 76\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9z+13 & \\ge 76 \\\\ 9z+13-13 & \\ge 76-13 \\\\ 9z & \\ge 63 \\\\ \\frac{9z}{9} & \\ge \\frac{63}{9} \\\\ z & \\ge 7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/4d/4d99dc1fe736da6fa15b96c62623d3d1f5eb6c716a36f5a8277a9f159edd0beb.png)\n\nTo find the values of $z$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/ac/ace8e5cfadcf29da623b01e653a9f201179aa643af00fe0759fd9619e0144ffb.png)\n\n \n\nThus, the final solution is $z\\ge 7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186646269 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34175e22-ddac-5d1e-9006-4dda6b32919a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645898} {:answer/id #uuid "7487710d-ee4c-5b37-9638-203bba104eec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186645975} {:answer/id #uuid "a0091bef-929f-567e-a612-1ee18600e887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186646043} {:answer/id #uuid "a1efa750-bd44-59d9-bd4c-fc5325146a17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186646047} {:answer/id #uuid "efaf3cad-a90e-542b-8806-0d2aa8dce430" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186646138}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186646047} :answer-field/id #uuid "607a7c08-aa92-5298-9a50-cc0eba0d112b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186646208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "17a2456e-4e43-5cf9-a581-23157022c089" :question/math-academy-id "q-97684" :question/problem "Lucy's marbles are labeled with numbers $5$ through $19.$ If Lucy chooses a marble at random, what is the probability that the marble number she picks is greater than $7$ and less than or equal to $10?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number on the chosen marble. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{5,6,…,19\\},$ and we wish to compute $P(7<X\\le 10).$\n\nIn general, if $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{5,6,…,19\\},$ and the set $S=\\{5,6,…,19\\}$ has $|S|=19-5+1=15$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{15}, & x=5,6,…,19 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $7<X\\le 10$ are $8,9,10.$ There are $3$ of these elements. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(7<X\\le 10)=3\\cdot \\frac{1}{15}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186651596 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80839318-77aa-5702-89d5-07fc0ae3cfed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cf/cffeec93aefb5a45fa3f0b9b8b876314dab329bbfd37111bc6ced3dda6d2bc37.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651248} {:answer/id #uuid "abc55ff6-c6b9-558b-807e-76ed59fe22dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/83/83d4750502e64980db6fcc0361d6d9233f0a9849aa253477997b32abf9077ebe.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651293} {:answer/id #uuid "b7eb926f-23b8-5765-b7ac-aefbb2dcf43c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/72/72d5063eaea57ea8ae7cfc5b5ede12cdbc2f45288bf141e130c1beaa745b4ad0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651314} {:answer/id #uuid "c9b3c0d6-3ab7-5e6b-8b86-403553a59e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/92/9204b9fe971eaf6a5aaae9ec9116f7d21083e31e2119d62e1642aa8bec6a9aa3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651348} {:answer/id #uuid "d98c02c4-2c04-5f4f-a3e9-825afcc6a8b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b4/b42e4590529951efc6abb9fd581997564d20f02d6e88ea8469dd6c9be1212d0f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651371}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186651348} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ed79ef4-b6ec-577a-aba1-689718a2ea11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7c022d67-ef84-55af-9af7-c4d946c3bf7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-174366" :question/problem "Which of the following is the indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ of the subset $A=\\{b,c,d\\}$ of $X=\\{a,b,c,d\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe indicator function of the set $\\{b,c,d\\}$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/f4/f4afa52dee6ffc5c42d95d684871dbedfb1445bbce5eabc6b9319e97ae6dafd2.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that the elements $b,c$ and $d$ (the elements of our subset) are mapped to $1,$ and all other elements are mapped to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186651613 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41b25d77-1eb8-59ea-be5e-7acfcd0c87fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{2,8\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651154} {:answer/id #uuid "5045941f-7cef-5741-9605-7a8e872511cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{2,4,6\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651173} {:answer/id #uuid "66201d08-4c6a-577c-a5a6-732130ef2fab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{0,2,8\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651204} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e39285-66b5-5d9c-8502-3ce577506c68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{0,2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651399} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4c909d-e589-5582-a2cf-10ef049436b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{0,4,6,8\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651410}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186651410} :answer-field/id #uuid "459bbd22-8f54-5292-a26a-eea493e91720" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186651464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "adb95551-8872-5707-9993-bc3c21a07949" :question/math-academy-id "q-174365" :question/problem "![](images/0c/0c72c8febda31280b9034e1efd92ad58dbdb2a63dc988d1dfb6fa437c6e61f8d.png)\n\nWhich of the following is the subset $A$ of $U=\\{0,2,4,6,8\\}$ whose indicator function ${1}_{A}(x)$ is shown above?" :question/worked-solution "An indicator function maps elements from a set to the values $0$ or $1,$ depending on whether the element belongs to a specified subset. The indicator function is designed to \"indicate\" whether an element is a member of a subset.\n\nMore specifically, consider a universal set $X.$ Then, the indicator function of a set $A⊆X$ is the function\n\n$$\n{1}_{A}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1, & \\text{if }x\\in A, \\\\ 0, & \\text{if }x\\notin A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the diagram above, only the elements $0,4,6$ and $8$ are mapped to $1.$ Therefore, the indicator function in the diagram above corresponds to the set $A=\\{0,4,6,8\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186652257 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed32b138-05e1-58c9-a5da-64c266391756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2e^{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186652095}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186652095} :answer-field/id #uuid "abbc21c5-fac2-5d89-9b78-f36f55da4f45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186652189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2e69817e-91f5-5459-8aeb-9a9c5ec713e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-340882" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=x{e}^{7{x}^{2}+2}$ for $x\\in [0,8),$ and let $f(x)$ be the **odd** extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in (-8,8).$ What is the value of $f(-2)?$\n\n$f(-2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [0,8),$ the odd extension of $F$ is the function $f$ such that\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}F(x), & x\\in [0,8), \\\\ -F(-x), & x\\in (-8,0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, for $x\\in (-\\pi ,0),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-F(-x) \\\\  & =-(-x){e}^{7(-x)^{2}+2} \\\\  & =x{e}^{7{x}^{2}+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =(-2){e}^{7(-2)^{2}+2}=-2{e}^{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653539 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cc6e4dd-01fe-5050-bf81-c9434e4e0274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653101} {:answer/id #uuid "25f74aeb-d80a-5b78-abbf-228c2b016473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653138} {:answer/id #uuid "5cb9383c-dc8e-50b5-8268-6064f6a300a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653222} {:answer/id #uuid "99cc1a89-7a4e-5afc-93d4-a1112388c331" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653298} {:answer/id #uuid "e22142a0-8475-576f-8518-856bea695baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653411}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653298} :answer-field/id #uuid "08542275-2c43-59f3-b828-5d330e276a8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3e1eecb6-c0fe-5351-9504-3810ed3c947b" :question/math-academy-id "q-96329" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,10],$ compute $P(-2\\le X<4).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,10],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20},\\, & -10\\le x\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2\\le X<4) & ={\\int }_{-2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{4}\\frac{1}{20}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4-(-2)}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653544 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f22385f-507d-5493-ae22-82d73cca1364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+2\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653154} {:answer/id #uuid "39941273-c169-5519-8829-21feef6806d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653173} {:answer/id #uuid "4fcc8a6b-4144-57ab-b7b7-1e588ec1dd1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653210} {:answer/id #uuid "c95c2a88-39f2-5a6c-bfba-93147793c05b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653366} {:answer/id #uuid "e81db107-f1a0-5691-b597-e3672139df09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653418}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653173} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cd2ff45-48df-5585-860e-194839f8bc8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "47b88c8d-12d5-598d-a0b6-a7675b7b1b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-96326" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\sqrt{2},0],$ compute $P(X\\ge -1).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\sqrt{2},0],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\, & -\\sqrt{2}\\le x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge -1) & =P(-1\\le X\\le 0) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(0-(-1))\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653550 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ff59810-21f2-5dca-9509-73eb7a47e50d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653156} {:answer/id #uuid "38bb11e8-e1cb-5c7c-b51b-a509793c2d73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653172} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3c7dac-3743-5384-9dd5-aabf8fe87725" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653175} {:answer/id #uuid "45841457-3150-5f88-b100-3162efadc2c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653189} {:answer/id #uuid "d271ac0c-a58c-5fcd-b020-08651f8fc217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653385}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653189} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccba682c-cf0a-5964-82fc-2ae7e67995ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "52d899b3-9c69-51b2-8189-9d8b17aa52e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-130542" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\frac{9}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}],$ compute $P(X<-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\frac{9}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & -\\frac{9}{2}\\le x\\le -\\frac{1}{2}, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-1) & =P(-\\frac{9}{2}\\le X<-1) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-9/2}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-9/2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{[-1-\\left(-\\frac{9}{2}\\right)]}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653554 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e6856ff-4056-5a18-8ae3-da993f467e5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653103} {:answer/id #uuid "3b50e22b-52bf-51ac-956e-1e67b4168a07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653178} {:answer/id #uuid "92f55975-d03c-5293-abae-3ccbeaaee23f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653289} {:answer/id #uuid "bad72738-6c95-5981-ab7e-152ef4973afa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653344} {:answer/id #uuid "c826e718-6859-5691-9f76-6b791c90b9b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653364}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653178} :answer-field/id #uuid "e81fd6a9-216e-5ba9-8dbd-21c65e442b6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "56c57e5f-ce9e-5732-9f03-c19bdf17e5aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-130547" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[4,7],$ compute $P(5\\le X<10).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[4,7],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3},\\, & 4\\le x\\le 7, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(5\\le X<10) & =P(5\\le x\\le 7) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{5}^{7}\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7-5}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06614678-50e4-5cc8-80ce-3f82e7c2efb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653672} {:answer/id #uuid "2169312c-8b38-518f-80bf-8e27319593de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653709} {:answer/id #uuid "6eafd665-1b5c-590b-90bb-295ba1d40807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653847} {:answer/id #uuid "ac890a88-e675-5fab-80d5-3771a33106db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653950} {:answer/id #uuid "c5dd8a2d-99df-5290-858d-0e1c94143bc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654003}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653709} :answer-field/id #uuid "76f7b399-8e2a-537e-bded-b63e87489887" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1a5de396-62ee-5a7a-a91b-fc346cbb4a9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-60742" :question/problem "Given the following piecewise function $f(x),$ what is $f(-1)?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+1\\,,\\, & x\\le -3 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\,,\\, & -3<x\\le 0 \\\\ -3x\\,,\\, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $x=-1$ is in the interval $-3<x\\le 0$, we use the middle branch, namely $f(x)={x}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) &=(-1)^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654251 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e025c6f-1068-5c67-b7dc-213b65718e5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8d/8dd6660aa289fc4ec03e08887a62efe7f49e55e1c89e96b1567cd6004adc8c66.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653681} {:answer/id #uuid "233a3129-72f1-586e-9038-fd3c6d3d9990" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/76/76a6511016c10df09224040e079fa5bc3b86c173be976ccb56f15c06ce1b0686.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653713} {:answer/id #uuid "3df5de68-ddba-5cb0-a473-d397cbfca3a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/91/9183f90c1fba993aab4c85ce71d39e23593155b399e5981a8fc1515e172abd29.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653762} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb4b27d-92eb-5410-8423-90d917dc6f48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/06/0637e4633ad60738346f5ab5cdb90bcc938a6f535040a9a85e7285256d5f56ed.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653799} {:answer/id #uuid "8cab1bcb-e766-5e43-9c64-e14ee8796e41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a7/a79ffdb2029a2dbe43a3c9ca41a977bdd22c69055d8631abe2665fbb2c54b15f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653895}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653799} :answer-field/id #uuid "1293cd6d-e29a-5b2b-9b06-b08cde6deea7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654130}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "202f248d-caa8-52da-b5ea-9c48dcd3738c" :question/math-academy-id "q-46789" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2\\,,\\, & x<-2 \\\\ 2\\,,\\, & x\\ge -2\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following is the graph of $y=f(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "We will graph each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,-2),$ we have $f(x)=-2,$ so the graph is a horizontal line that ends at $(-2,-2),$ excluding this point.\n\n- On the interval $[-2,\\infty )$, we have $f(x)=2$, so the graph is a horizontal line that begins at $(-2,2),$ including this point.\n\nTherefore, the graph of the given function is as follows:\n\n![](images/06/0637e4633ad60738346f5ab5cdb90bcc938a6f535040a9a85e7285256d5f56ed.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654254 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43be9764-5399-5517-a2f0-39f74cb9f595" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653774} {:answer/id #uuid "b49f1ba3-3082-5359-8b4a-766decd9b2cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653967} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f5d1f0-2877-5d75-bccf-14ec440759cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654013} {:answer/id #uuid "cbd858d0-e023-5841-93a2-5279eb7696d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654017} {:answer/id #uuid "e30058c8-06f5-5976-b44c-6513f6bfb948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654062}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653967} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ecc4506-d737-5003-8c71-f0bef9e7a6cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e57df09-166b-527d-998c-2b7b75e7184a" :question/math-academy-id "q-19301" :question/problem "Given the following piecewise function $f(x),$ what is $f(1)?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4}x,\\, & x\\le 2 \\\\ 2,\\, & x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $x=1$ is in the interval $x\\le 2,$ we use the left-hand branch, namely $f(x)=-\\frac{3}{4}x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =-\\frac{3}{4}(1)=-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654263 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d907b28-458b-5bac-800c-f4ef53d8f1ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+1,\\, & x\\le -1 \\\\ -x+1,\\, & x>-1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653760} {:answer/id #uuid "537c5f04-8552-52b7-8456-64d1199c8374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x-1,\\, & x\\le -1 \\\\ -x+1,\\, & x>-1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653805} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3862e8-aa1e-5050-81ad-d35378e76daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The graph is not a function" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653914} {:answer/id #uuid "9cb01de4-066c-55a2-b622-c5cc5335dab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+1,\\, & x\\le -2 \\\\ -x-1,\\, & x>-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653915} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc0fe7a-1cab-52e0-9712-3e6c8b57e298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+1,\\, & x\\le -2 \\\\ x-1,\\, & x>-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654019}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653760} :answer-field/id #uuid "f76dc602-64b2-5f16-8037-99d289c94317" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "40f55d54-ca28-5d0c-b3b7-b8a8573ffc3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-7290" :question/problem "![](images/ee/ee3854972fcefe83938f8c0f12937c430cb5faf8fdaf789e44799a870fedc95d.png)\n\nWhat is the definition of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We will graph each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,-1]$, we have a line with a slope of $1$ that passes through the point $(-1,0).$ We can find the equation of this line using point-slope form:\n\n$$\ny-0=1(x-(-1))\\,⟹\\,y=x+1\n$$\n\nSo the graph is the line $y=x+1$ that ends at $(-1,0),$ including this point.\n\n- On the interval $(-1,\\infty ),$ we have a line with a slope of $-1$ and $y$-intercept $1.$ So the graph is the line $y=-x+1$ that starts at $(-1,2),$ excluding this point.\n\nTherefore, the function is defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+1,\\, & x\\le -1 \\\\ -x+1,\\, & x>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654268 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1764ff0a-9621-5510-bd9d-fd19d7a206cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653696} {:answer/id #uuid "297d366d-2d0e-5296-a77b-76f809405f59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653720} {:answer/id #uuid "2cc51558-1966-548b-bea2-2b7b560912df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653727} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b63b52-d161-54a6-bd31-914c8f0df886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654067} {:answer/id #uuid "fc16100f-81f6-582f-901d-162d0e76b72f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654116}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653720} :answer-field/id #uuid "16c52b83-f7c1-50c9-97b4-dbde1d9c1c8c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654131}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4f6da749-4788-57e6-94d5-fec27205f7dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-126174" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1, \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{8}, & 1\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 1, & x>3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(1<X<2).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that for continuous random variables, it doesn't matter whether or not we include the endpoints of the interval. So we can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X<2) & =P(1<X\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)-P(X\\le 1) \\\\  & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}-1}{8}-\\frac{{1}^{2}-1}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "551d93d1-b1bc-583e-bd0a-b86d5c8e2afe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{e}^{3x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653810} {:answer/id #uuid "973f8225-7fd8-50e5-ae5b-3647cf52f02f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653909} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea501f4-f5ee-5307-9948-0b5ca1947e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653920} {:answer/id #uuid "c99b2cba-d5d7-5c96-a3e5-9e3ac73ecf2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654012} {:answer/id #uuid "db4ea894-b49c-5de8-82cf-2525c69b05e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654047}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654047} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc682ec0-a4eb-5442-b24d-8e52c4f33081" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "648419e9-760a-5b7e-a483-68e287bf40e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-126206" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-|3x|},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}h(x),\\, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{2},\\, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the function $h(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that involves an absolute value, the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x<0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t, & x\\ge 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the integrals.\n\n- If $x\\le 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{x}\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3t}|}_{-\\infty }^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $x>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-3t}|}_{0}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{2}, & x<0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{2}, & x\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654290 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03f4a238-3e9a-5b66-9a21-bfe56260c705" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+3,\\, & x\\le 3 \\\\ 3,\\, & x>3\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653668} {:answer/id #uuid "0e2c74b6-457f-5af2-ad28-d83fc3d7a4b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x-3,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ -3,\\, & x>1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653683} {:answer/id #uuid "62397c06-9a13-5e71-863a-1c4c685416a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3,\\, & x\\le 0 \\\\ x+3,\\, & x>0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653826} {:answer/id #uuid "75123113-a5ef-5aa1-a3ee-dc7d216055b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3,\\, & x\\le 3 \\\\ x-3,\\, & x>3\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653861} {:answer/id #uuid "b7783651-b167-57e1-a493-4596cad67499" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+3,\\, & x\\le 0 \\\\ -3,\\, & x>0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653973}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653668} :answer-field/id #uuid "4298802c-5bb7-55aa-a3f6-68fa3e896301" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8d9ce15a-205c-5d81-a94e-7bf91fb65cdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-79552" :question/problem "![](images/f4/f4ceaa1ef03b5149720b28ae9b7b59927e8d4c04107547051663373a859132e6.png)\n\nWhat is the definition of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We will graph each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,3],$ we have a line with a slope of $-1$ and $y$-intercept $3.$ So the graph is the line $y=-x+3$ that ends at $(3,0),$ including this point.\n\n- On the interval $(3,\\infty ),$ we have a horizontal line that passes through the point $(3,3).$ So the graph is the line $y=3$ that starts at $(3,3),$ excluding this point.\n\nTherefore, the function is defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+3,\\, & x\\le 3 \\\\ 3,\\, & x>3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1749739b-5598-599b-ba78-5f69b3650b8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-1\\,,\\, & x\\le 0 \\\\ 1\\,,\\, & x>0\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653695} {:answer/id #uuid "90f9f1e9-baac-5dd6-aeb3-ad14fc3e2cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2\\,,\\, & x<1 \\\\ 2\\,,\\, & x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653905} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ff710a-62ac-5658-9675-bd6d4cfe6675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2\\,,\\, & x\\le 1 \\\\ -2\\,,\\, & x>1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653996} {:answer/id #uuid "de3b9dc0-a1a2-5703-916c-9ef21bb79281" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-1\\,,\\, & x<2 \\\\ 1\\,,\\, & x\\ge 2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654053} {:answer/id #uuid "ea1f126c-2071-5c74-9fe4-350e2e543f65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1\\,,\\, & x<2 \\\\ -1\\,,\\, & x\\ge 2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654078}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654053} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f6ca781-e314-54e3-bb2c-5f145260d2e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654149}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a1f0c6b9-dd5f-5ffc-8878-0999104167a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-46885" :question/problem "![](images/a6/a64c079b8af048a98e06d90c0c498cfe214291d62b7447f900f146c0a69d191d.png)\n\nWhat's the definition of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above, given that $f(x)$ is defined for $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )?$" :question/worked-solution "We will determine each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,2),$ we have $f(x)=-1.$ Notice that the point $x=2$ is excluded.\n\n- On the interval $[2,\\infty )$, we have $f(x)=1.$ Notice that the point $x=2$ is included.\n\nHence the definition of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-1\\,,\\, & x<2 \\\\ 1\\,,\\, & x\\ge 2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33658db0-50f3-5f64-828e-c68312733b05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x-6,\\, & x\\le -2 \\\\ -x,\\, & x>-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653739} {:answer/id #uuid "5828bdd3-6096-58f9-a1cc-fa00fdb96115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x-2,\\, & x\\le -2 \\\\ -x,\\, & x>-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653813} {:answer/id #uuid "594a7ad5-2a28-5e5e-bcc0-9bf4d43cec02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x-4,\\, & x\\le -2 \\\\ x,\\, & x>-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653816} {:answer/id #uuid "8ac81046-1d64-5cf4-babe-5fb899d27c7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x-6,\\, & x\\le -2 \\\\ x,\\, & x>-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653889} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8a3b97-6c1d-5525-bb7d-b854554e7515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x-10,\\, & x\\le -2 \\\\ -x,\\, & x>-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654015}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186654015} :answer-field/id #uuid "af8fbd3b-df33-54c0-a424-36239a5af212" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186654196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "b1b635ac-b706-5d28-bb8d-a8a3ba49a674" :question/math-academy-id "q-129283" :question/problem "![](images/35/35e8405299115fc5796655516f737c372d74a932a966a717502359b7ac1cadca.png)\n\nWhat is the definition of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "We will graph each branch separately.\n\n- On the interval $(-\\infty ,-2],$ we have a line with a slope of $-4$ that passes through the point $(-2,-2).$ We can find the equation of this line using the point-slope form:\n\n$$\ny-(-2)=-4(x-(-2))\\,⟹\\,y=-4x-10\n$$\n\nSo the graph is the line $y=-4x-10$ that ends at $(-2,-2),$ including this point.\n\n- On the interval $(-2,\\infty ),$ we have a line with slope $-1$ and $y$-intercept $0.$ So the graph is the line $y=-x$ that starts at $(-2,2),$ excluding this point.\n\nTherefore, the function is defined as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x-10,\\, & x\\le -2 \\\\ -x,\\, & x>-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
